    "updated_at": "2021-09-13T06:34:25Z",
    "body": "On the one hand it makes sense for it to be non-normative as there's nothing there we need implementations to implement, but then we would need a definition that stands on its own. As it stands it seems more like a normative dependency, at least for the \"meaning\" part.\r\n\r\nI suspect Ian prefixed it with \"internet\" since the IETF came up with that definition, but not sure. Seems fine to drop it.",
